// error: what is passed for `action` of `Barrier` may use only sendable values from around it, but it captures `rounds`, a `var`, which the closure would share with the code that made it; copy it into a `val`, or share it through an `Atomic` or a `Mutex`
// error: what is passed for `action` of `Barrier` may use only sendable values from around it, but it uses `seen`, a `Buffer[int]`, which is mutable; an immutable copy (`toVector`) is sendable
// error: what is passed for `value` of `RwLock` may use only sendable values from around it, but it uses `kept`, a `Buffer[int]`, which is mutable; an immutable copy (`toVector`) is sendable
// error: what is passed for `body` of `RwLock.write` may use only sendable values from around it, but it uses `seen`, a `Buffer[int]`, which is mutable; an immutable copy (`toVector`) is sendable
// error: `Buffer[int]` does not conform to `Sendable`, the bound of `R` in `read`: it is mutable; an immutable copy (`toVector`) is sendable
// A barrier's action runs on whichever thread arrives last, so it captures only sendable values; a
// read-write lock's value and bodies are isolating, as a mutex's are, so nothing reaches the value but
// through the lock.
import avin.threads.{Barrier, RwLock}

main()
  var rounds = 0
  val seen = Buffer[int]()
  val b = Barrier(2, () -> rounds += 1)
  val c = Barrier(2, () -> seen.append(1))
  val kept = Buffer[int]()
  val l = RwLock(kept)
  val m = RwLock(Buffer[int]())
  m.write(v -> v.append(seen.length))
  m.read(v -> seen)
